It talks to the official XRPC API of the AT Protocol (https://docs.bsky.app,
lexicons of https://github.com/bluesky-social/atproto) with an app password
of one Bluesky account. This integration is unofficial: it is not affiliated
with nor endorsed by Bluesky Social PBC. Bluesky and the butterfly logo are
trademarks of Bluesky Social PBC.

The butterfly of the cover (docs/assets/cover.svg, cover.jpg) is the official
Bluesky logo, its path copied unchanged from
https://github.com/bluesky-social/social-app/blob/main/bskyembed/assets/logo.svg
(repository under the MIT License; the logo itself remains a trademark of
Bluesky Social PBC). The rest of the cover is an illustration.

It depends on:
  - @gladysassistant/integration-sdk (Apache License 2.0).

Design inspiration, read only, no code copied:
  - the documentation of Bluesky (docs.bsky.app): rich text facets in UTF-8
    bytes, rate limits, API hosts and the chat proxy;
  - the official app bluesky-social/social-app (MIT License): the polling of
    chat.bsky.convo.getLog by `rev`, and the "Bad token method" answer of an
    app password without access to direct messages;
  - the Slack integration for Gladys of the same author: linking a chat
    account with a code sent in a direct message.
